1
00:00:00,870 --> 00:00:02,020
Lambert ordered you out?

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:03,640
Just like that?

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,580
My daughter was dead.

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,840
And how does that take precedence
over matters of national security?

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,800
It doesn't.

6
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,580
So you agree Lambert
made a judgment error?

7
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,360
I won't answer that.

8
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:17,940
Fine.

9
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,330
So the little information
you did recover from Iceland told you

10
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,720
that what was stolen
from Raheem Kadir was not a weapon at all.

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,010
It was Red Mercury, right?
Yes.

12
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:31,730
An explosive substance which,
when added to small doses of plutonium,

13
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,350
can easily create a two-kiloton bomb
the size of a baseball.

14
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,760
And you and Lambert lost it.

15
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:40,190
We had a lead, Emile Dufraisne.

16
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:43,700
He tried to buy the Red Mercury
before it was stolen.

17
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:47,200
So Lambert decided
to infiltrate Dufraisne's organization,

18
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,160
hoping he'd take another shot
at getting his hands on the Red Mercury.

19
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,520
That's why he sent you in,

20
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:57,460
undercover on American soil,
clearly exceeding the NSA's mandate.

21
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:01,240
Our mandate is to protect
American citizens.

22
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:03,530
The CIA was dragging its feet.

23
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,640
It was us or nobody.

24
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,660
But to infiltrate Dufraisne's
organization, you needed a way in.

25
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:12,860
And you found it
at Ellsworth Penitentiary.
